{{- /*
Context polix injects on every session start of a valid polix.yaml, agent neutral, as the agent reads it: the header
lines, then the "- " items on commits, the root and the folders of the AI, with no blank lines; the whole text is
trimmed. Each line is concise and at most 120 characters with the default folders and a short root (a test checks
it): split a rule into several items rather than wrap it.
Data: .Root (the root of the working tree, with forward slashes) and .Path (the folder of the AI, path of
polix.yaml cleaned, relative to the root, without a trailing slash; ai by default).
*/ -}}
This project is managed by polix.
Follow these rules:
- Run each git commit as a command of its own: never chain it with &&, ; or |, nor wrap it in sh -c or bash -c.
- Pass the commit message with -m, -F or a heredoc inside -m.
- Otherwise polix does not recognise the commit and skips its pre_commit gates.
- The root of the project is {{.Root}}.
- Use these folders, below the root, and no other paths:
  - {{.Path}}/rules/: the rules on how to write the code, one yaml file per topic.
  - {{.Path}}/plans/: the implementation plans, one per file.
  - {{.Path}}/reports/: the reports of audits and reviews, one per file.
  - {{.Path}}/tasks/: the backlog of tasks, one per file.
